## Lore

The Q''uratigo Cephalopodans, known to nearly everyone as Kraks (a slur on
Kraken Men that they cheerfully adopted), are short, hairless, green, tan
or brown D-Bees with big expressive eyes and a pair of fleshy tentacles
hanging from the nasal ridge like a drooping mustache. Behind the tentacles
is a startlingly human mouth, and they run to potbellies and wrinkles with
age.

Kraks are born mimics. Within weeks of arriving somewhere they pick up the
local accent, slang, dress and gestures, and in a group they tend to copy
whoever they admire most, to that person''s occasional annoyance. All of
them in North America are three or four generations removed from whatever
Rift brought them, most likely in Alaska, and nine in ten consider
themselves Earthlings, or Canadians, or Americans. Their tales of a warm,
marshy Old Planet survive mostly as contradictory family traditions.

They are friendly, loud, social and usually working class: vagabonds,
operators, salvagers, scouts, pilots and drivers, with a handful in smuggling
and the Black Market. Some humans find them delightful; the Coalition and
Free Quebec see their very human manner as a dangerous act.

## GM Notes

The book heads the race an optional player character or NPC.

Size 3 to 4 feet (0.9 to 1.2 m). Weight 85 to 180 pounds (38 to 81 kg).
Life span 4D6+100 years. Slave market value 1D4x1,000 credits, low demand.

Habitat: mainly the far northwest (Canada and Alaska) and eastern Siberia,
adapted to land and cold.

Allies: anyone who will put up with them; Larmac, Devil Men, Dog Boys,
Idie, Fingertooth Carpetbaggers, Shapers and Fennodi. Enemies: bigots and
the plainly evil; they avoid the Minions of Splugorth, Vanguard Brawlers,
Coalition soldiers and predatory slayer types.
